{"ts": 1791651077.3362172, "run_id": "20261010_165117_a346bd0b", "trace_id": "20261010_165117_a346bd0b", "session_id": "swe-20261010_165117-d9bf6c9f", "agent_id": "agent-9fd39d79", "parent_agent_id": null, "parent_trace_id": null, "agent_type": "main", "event": "benchmark_instance", "instance_id": "sympy__sympy-22914", "benchmark_profile": "verified", "prompt": "Solve SWE-bench Verified instance `sympy__sympy-22914`.\nRepository: sympy/sympy\nBase commit: c4e836cdf73fc6aa7bab6a86719a0f08861ffb1d\n\nProblem statement:\nPythonCodePrinter doesn't support Min and Max\nWe can't generate python code for the sympy function Min and Max.\r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n```\r\nfrom sympy import symbols, Min, pycode\r\na, b = symbols(\"a b\")\r\nc = Min(a,b)\r\nprint(pycode(c))\r\n```\r\nthe output is:\r\n\r\n```\r\n  # Not supported in Python:\r\n  # Min\r\nMin(a, b)\r\n```\r\n\r\nSimilar to issue #16669, we should add following methods to PythonCodePrinter:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndef _print_Min(self, expr):\r\n    return \"min({})\".format(\", \".join(self._print(arg) for arg in expr.args))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _print_Max(self, expr):\r\n    return \"max({})\".format(\", \".join(self._print(arg) for arg in expr.args))\r\n\r\n```\n\nWhen finished, leave the repository with only the intended source-code changes.", "strict": true, "attempts": 1}
